            <ArticleTitle>Direct arylation catalysis with chloro[8-(dimesitylboryl)quinoline-κN]copper(I).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2757-2762</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3762/bjoc.12.272</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report direct arylation of arylhalides with unactivated sp2 C-H bonds in benzene and naphthalene using a copper(I) catalyst featuring an ambiphilic ligand, (quinolin-8-yl)dimesitylborane. Direct arylation could be achieved with 0.2 mol % catalyst and 3 equivalents of base (KO(t-Bu)) at 80 °C to afford TON ≈160-190 over 40 hours.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
